speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, there have been discussions among the parties and I think you would find that there would be unanimous consent for the following motion to be put and voted upon without debate. I move:
That, immediately after the completion of Routine Proceedings, the House will proceed to Orders of the Day for debate on the motion for second reading of Bill C-62; and
That, following the speech on the said motion by the Minister of Finance, further proceedings this day on the said motion and any amendment thereto be as follows and in this sequence:
-a speech (without time limit) by both of the Leader or designated spokesperson of each of the Official Opposition and the New Democratic Party;
-a period of one hour for questions and comment, directed to the Minister of Finance, along the format used in Question Period;
-a deemed adjournment of debate, without further debate or question put, on the said motion and any amendment thereto;
-a deemed adjournment of the House until eleven o'clock a.m., Thesday, January 30, 1990, without further debate or question put on such motion for adjournment;
- Provided that, for the remainder of this day, no dilatory motion shall be receivable by the Chair.
